        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T18:10:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This `flags` field doesn\u0027t seem very useful, we could just always use GFP_KERNEL_ACCOUNT and kvm_account_pgtable_pages() in pkvm_mc_alloc_fn() instead? That would simplify the code (for instance, init_pkvm_stage2_memcache() would not be needed).\n\nI know pKVM-ARM uses it (BTW it doesn\u0027t seem quite useful there either), but we don\u0027t need to make the code more complicated than needed just to keep it the same as in the (current snapshot of) pKVM-ARM code?",
      "revId": "ee62f287569a29449ff811011b45661515146dbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e304a5c_b80e4ca9",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 748,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-26T22:28:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general pkvm_memcache\u0027s are not only used for guest ept pgtables but also for different purposes (before this series). Setting extra HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_STAGE2 indicates using generic kvm mechanism for accounting page tables pages kvm_account_pgtable_pages which should happen only for stage2 memcaches (e.g re-use `pkvm_mc_free_fn` which correctly decrease counters only for stage2 memcache, not for other memcaches.)\n\nBTW kvm_account_pgtable_pages is actually very useful and allowed me to find and fix some bugs with leaking page on early implementation of this patchset.\n\nBut I think dropping HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_KMEMCG is an good idea.",
      "parentUuid": "75cd0329_cf0ad8ef",
      "revId": "ee62f287569a29449ff811011b45661515146dbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85119df3_fa9309ec",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 748,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T13:51:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, ok... My point was that we\u0027re not gonna reuse pkvm_mc_alloc_fn() for other (non-MMU) stuff, so it seems better to keep it simple and adjusted to the MMU use case.\n\nNow I see, we don\u0027t reuse pkvm_mc_alloc_fn() but we do reuse pkvm_mc_free_fn() for non-MMU stuff.\n\nSo, ok, let\u0027s keep doing it pKVM-ARM way (even though it seems a bit too fancy: so many ways to customize such a simple thing as pkvm_memcache: custom `alloc_fn` callback, custom `to_pa` callback, custom `flags`...)\n\nSpeaking of details:\n\n1. So, these pkvm_mc_alloc_fn()/pkvm_mc_free_fn(), as well as topup_pkvm_memcache() and free_pkvm_memcache(), are not really MMU-specific, so they don\u0027t really belong in mmu.c? It seems cleaner to put them in a pKVM-specific file (which, at the same time, is a part of host code, not hypervisor code). In 6.12 that would be, for example, arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm.c (and in 6.15+, for example, arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c)?\n\nIt might be a minor issue, but I\u0027d prefer to minimize the amount of pKVM-specific code in this common KVM\u0027s mmu.c (especially such code that is not strictly MMU-related and thus doesn\u0027t really belong there).\n\n2. Regarding HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_STAGE2: rename it e.g. to PKVM_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_SECONDARY?\n\n3. Regarding dropping HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_KMEMCG: yeah, it seems a good idea, given that, it appears, we also always use GFP_KERNEL_ACCOUNT when allocating any pages that we free via `teardown_mc` later.",
      "parentUuid": "9e304a5c_b80e4ca9",
      "revId": "ee62f287569a29449ff811011b45661515146dbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "016f8504_0e3dd674",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
