        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T18:10:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Similarly to my comment about `stage2_mc` in aosp/3702535, we could name this e.g. `guest_mmu_teardown_mc`?\n\n...Or actually, why do we even need this separate memcache? Can\u0027t we reuse `teardown_mc`?",
      "revId": "ee62f287569a29449ff811011b45661515146dbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea6fa4d2_ea41f8fa",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 823,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-26T22:28:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need separate one, since it is initialized with HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_STAGE2, which results with properly tracking and accounting kvm_account_pgtable_pages (the counter is decreased during free_pkvm_memcache if this flag is set) which shouldn\u0027t happen for `teardown_mc`. Again, I\u0027ve found it very useful for validating and fixing bugs related to leak of page-table pages during teardown by checking the page-table page counter (monitoring `/proc/meminfo`\u0027s`SecPageTables` before vm started, and after vm teardown -\u003e BTW I will also add it to the `TEST:` tag in commit log).\n\n`guest_mmu_teardown_mc` sounds ok, but maybe emphasizing that this is stage-2 and call it `guest_ept_teardown_mc` or `guest_tdp_teardown_mc` (tdp to cover both Intel ept and potential AMD npt), WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "bbae1fc3_7e929419",
      "revId": "ee62f287569a29449ff811011b45661515146dbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "be864f59_287dcf30",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
